# Jarvis brain: the same weights as the base model, loaded so it actually fits.
#
# Why this file exists. Ollama 0.34 loads ``qwen3:4b`` with a 65536-token context
# by default. On this machine that is fatal: the KV cache inflates the model to
# ~13 GB, only 16% of it fits in the 4 GB GPU, and the rest runs on the CPU at
# roughly 6 tokens per second -- so a single spoken question exceeds any sane
# timeout. Measured with ``ollama ps`` and the timings in ``/api/chat``:
#
#   context 65536 -> 13 GB resident -> 84%/16% CPU/GPU -> 6 tok/s
#
# An 8k context is far more than a spoken turn needs (the system prompt is ~700
# tokens and the tool schemas ~3300) while keeping the model resident in VRAM.
#
# Create it once; ``scripts\setup.ps1`` does this for you:
#
#   ollama create jarvis-brain:4b -f config\ollama\Modelfile.jarvis
#
# Pointing JARVIS_OLLAMA_MODEL at this name is what keeps Jarvis responsive. The
# base model is still what gets pulled; this only changes how it is loaded.

FROM qwen3:4b

PARAMETER num_ctx 8192
PARAMETER temperature 0.2
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
